      "content": "i get that it's a myth, but i've been reading some of the older medical texts used in training that actually suggest physiological differences in how certain ethnicities process pain or react to anesthesia. like, if i'm looking at old-school clinical studies or historical data, why would those patterns have been documented so frequently if there's no biological basis for it? is it possible there are subtle physiological variations that current modern medicine just hasn't fully accounted for yet?",
